          "text": "Clinical Indication:  \nHistory of focal epilepsy with focal aware seizures, onset at age 24, occurring approximately 5 times per week. Etiology is unknown. Drug-resistant epilepsy. Current antiseizure medications: perampanel, lamotrigine, topiramate, and brivaracetam.\n\nTechnique:  \nRoutine scalp EEG obtained using standard electrode placement and conventional longitudinal and transverse bipolar montages, with recording of the available waking state.\n\nFindings:  \nNo specific interictal or ictal EEG findings are provided in the available report data.\n\nImpression:  \nThis report is limited by the absence of supplied EEG waveform findings. Clinical history is notable for drug-resistant focal epilepsy with focal aware seizures beginning at age 24, occurring approximately five times weekly, with unknown etiology. Current medications are perampanel, lamotrigine, topiramate, and brivaracetam.",
